You have an App Service app named orders-web that serves the custom domain orders.contoso.com over HTTPS through a TLS binding. The app builds absolute URLs that it returns to browsers and hands to a payment provider, and users report that these links start with http:// even though they reached the site over https://. The incoming connection is already decrypted before the request is handed to the app process (see the exhibit). You need the generated absolute URLs to reflect the protocol that the client actually used. Which change should you make to the app code?

`// OrdersController
public string BuildCallbackUrl()
{
    // The scheme reported here is always "http":
    // the connection was decrypted before the request reached this process.
    return Request.Scheme + "://" + Request.Host.Value + "/api/payments/callback";
}`

